# Draft (2026-10-17). Add `date-released` and `doi` when v0.4.1 is tagged and archived.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "csid: a Wi-Fi channel state information capture daemon and the CSIQ format"
abstract: >-
  A systemd-native Wi-Fi Channel State Information capture daemon for Intel AX210 radios on
  Linux 6.x, and CSIQ, a self-describing and versioned interchange format for CSI with reference
  readers in Rust and Python. Every session writes a sidecar with the radio configuration,
  firmware, kernel, driver module, regulatory domain and governor before capture starts.
authors:
  - family-names: Dubec
    given-names: Jakub
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4248-5264"
    affiliation: "Slovak University of Technology in Bratislava, Faculty of Informatics and Information Technologies"
version: "0.4.1"
license: GPL-2.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sibyx/csid"
keywords:
  - channel state information
  - Wi-Fi sensing
  - Intel AX210
  - measurement instrument
  - CSIQ
